---
const GAPS = [
  {
    title: "The result arrives",
    copy: "A partner lab posts a fasting glucose or an LDL. It is filed in a system that was built to store results, not to chase them.",
  },
  {
    title: "Nobody owns the next step",
    copy: "The patient assumes the clinic will call. The clinic assumes the patient will book. The gap between those two assumptions is the loop.",
  },
  {
    title: "The record closes silently",
    copy: "Thirty days later the case is still open, nobody can say whether it was communicated, and the audit trail starts with a phone note.",
  },
];
---

<section class="border-y border-canvas-line bg-canvas-raised py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <div class="max-w-2xl" data-animate>
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent-strong">
        The gap
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-extrabold text-ink sm:text-4xl">
        Most abnormal results are not missed. They are unowned.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        A screening programme is only as good as its follow-up. Hermes exists to
        make the follow-up a designed workflow with a clock, an owner and an
        audit trail instead of a best effort between two busy teams.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3" data-stagger>
      {
        GAPS.map((gap, index) => (
          <li class="rounded-lg border border-canvas-line bg-canvas p-6">
            <span class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-accent-strong">
              0{index + 1}
            </span>
            <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">
              {gap.title}
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
              {gap.copy}
            </p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
